{# Transcribed from the static design mockup (pre-checkout page), STEP PROGRESS section
   (completed/checkmark connector variant verified against the medical page). Parameterized:
   `steps` (list of {label, icon}), `active` (1-based index of the active step), and
   optional `progress` ({after, fill_id, label_id, percent}) — the connector AFTER step
   `progress.after` renders as the fill-bar variant with the given element ids and
   percent. Steps before `active` render completed (bg-secondary + checkmark
   connector); the active step renders bg-primary; steps after render bg-divider.

   The three states share one block rather than being written out three times.
   They diverge only in two class strings and in what the connector draws, and
   the copies had already drifted: a step's markup is the thing
   theme/js/intake.js re-points as the visitor moves between pages, so there is
   exactly one shape for it to know about.

   `step.icon` is optional. A step derived from a form page ({@see
   AsterMD\Storefront\Forms\ProgressSteps}) has a position and no meaning to
   draw, so it renders its number; a funnel step names a lucide icon and draws
   that.

   Each label is absolutely centered under its own icon (left-1/2 + -translate-x-1/2)
   instead of living in a matching-width flex column — flex items default to
   min-width:auto, so a fixed-width label column would silently grow to fit
   "Verify & Review" and stop lining up under its circle. Labels wrap within a
   fixed w-20 box (no whitespace-nowrap) so "Verify & Review" breaks onto two
   lines instead of overflowing past the viewport edge on narrow screens. #}
{% set circle_classes = {
  'done':   'bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground',
  'active': 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground',
  'todo':   'bg-divider text-muted',
} %}
{% set label_classes = {
  'done':   'font-medium text-heading',
  'active': 'font-medium text-primary',
  'todo':   'text-muted',
} %}
<div class="mx-auto max-w-[660px] px-6 pb-10 pt-10" data-funnel-stepper>
  <div class="flex items-center">
    {% for step in steps %}
      {% set i = loop.index %}
      {% set state = i < active ? 'done' : (i == active ? 'active' : 'todo') %}
      <div class="relative shrink-0" data-stepper-step="{{ i }}">
        <span data-stepper-circle class="flex size-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full {{ circle_classes[state] }}">
          {% if step.icon %}
            <i data-lucide="{{ step.icon }}" class="size-5"></i>
          {% else %}
            <span class="text-base font-semibold">{{ i }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </span>
        <span data-stepper-label class="absolute left-1/2 top-full mt-2 w-20 -translate-x-1/2 text-center text-sm leading-tight {{ label_classes[state] }}">{{ step.label }}</span>
      </div>

      {% if not loop.last %}
        {% if progress is defined and progress and progress.after == i %}
          <div class="relative mx-2 h-0.5 flex-1 bg-border" data-stepper-connector="{{ i }}">
            <div id="{{ progress.fill_id }}" class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 bg-primary" style="width: {{ progress.percent }}%"></div>
            <span id="{{ progress.label_id }}" class="absolute inset-x-0 -top-6 text-center text-xs font-medium text-primary">{{ progress.percent }}%</span>
          </div>
        {% else %}
          <div class="relative mx-2 h-0.5 flex-1 {{ i < active ? 'bg-secondary' : 'bg-border' }}" data-stepper-connector="{{ i }}">
            <span data-stepper-tick class="absolute inset-x-0 -top-6 text-center text-sm text-heading{{ i < active ? '' : ' hidden' }}">&#10003;</span>
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
